$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @	
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 1.5" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamster" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Larua" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Mahkali" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> January 15th, 4025" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Brunt" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 6" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 32" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! While patrolling the airs above the city of Jura, we have been attacked by a similar enemy stronghold! During the last several days, the fighting has been fierce. Our engineers have constructed a bridge to the enemy base and have tried to erect defenses on it, but the enemy is attempting to re-route its team recognition in order to gain control of it and use it against us! I know you are fresh off the reinforcement drop-ship, but this is no boot camp! If we loose control of the airways in this region, it will severely weaken our control of Larua, the major supply planet in this sector! Millions of lives could ultimately rest on your shoulders, so fight bravely. Your tribe is counting on you!\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>Gain control of the center bridge ASAP. It will protect you from most frontal assaults, especially early in the game.\nIf your team looses control of the center and is having trouble regaining it, disable the gen to take down the defenses, or use the roof mortar (or another coordinated mortar strike) to destroy the turrets.\nTry to keep the center in working order when it is under your control.\nA frontal assault is not the only type.\nEach team has two sets of inv and gens. If one goes down and is being watched by the enemy, try to get the other set working.\n\n<f1>Version History<f0>\nVers. 1.5\nUpdated contact info.\n\nVers. 1.4\nUpdated (.dsc) description file.\nChanged cap limit from default to 6.\n\nVers. 1.3\nAdded Map Markers.\nFixed so Center switch has name.\n\nVers. 1.2\nMoved middle elevator in the hopes of avoiding jams.\nMoved back of base platforms to make them easier to navigate.\n\nVers. 1.1\nRearranged platforms connecting bases to ground to make them slightly less impossible.\nFixed middle elevator jams.\nRedesigned middle outposts for optimum sniping.\nAltered base plasma turrets.\nRotated one of teams vehicle pad to face in the correct direction.\nAdded structure and items on ground.\nMoved base rear solar panels to make them harder to destroy.\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";

